  **scale-down score-weighted PRC tie-break**, which is an *ordering* key, not the
  fair-share metric — invariant 11 permits a ranking weight there. They are not
  false after C6c. But they now *read* as contradicting C6c's new "score takes no
  part in fair share" prose, which I think is why the inventory caught them, so I
  added one clarifying clause at the canonical definition site
